  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nTonight through next Thursday...A dry cold front is in the process \nof moving through the CWA this afternoon. Other than an increase in \ncloud cover, very little to no shower activity is forecast to \naccompany this front.  Strong high pressure building into the \nforecast area in its wake, is resulting in a tight pressure gradient \nacross the region. These gusty northwest winds are ushering in a \nnoticeably cooler drier airmass, that'll linger across the CWA \nthrough the weekend. While pleasant early fall conditions will exist \nduring this time, temperatures will steadily warm across the region \nnext week. However, the dry airmass will remain. Thus, resulting in \nless humid conditions throughout this forecast period.\n\nOnce again on Saturday, a significant threat of dangerous fire \nweather conditions will exist across the forecast area.  Soil \nconditions remain critically dry, with no rain chances in site. \nBreezy northerly winds will also promote a very dry airmass across \nthe region.  While lower high temperatures on Saturday will yield \nslightly higher afternoon minimum relative humidity values compared \nto today, humidity values will still fall to near critical levels at \naround 30-35% across nearly all of the area.  Therefore, I've \nupgraded the \"Fire Weather Watch\" to a \"Red Flag Warning\" for \nSaturday on this afternoon's package.  Today's \"Red Flag Warning\" is \nin effect until 8 PM CDT. /19/",
